  "findings": [
    "Task/region identities and dependencies matter; identical source-level loop bodies need not have identical trace arguments.",
    "Online history mining, trace memoization and actual task execution are separate costs. Longer traces reduce fixed replay work but can expose waiting and replay-issue latency.",
    "Distributed asynchronous results must be ingested consistently across replicated control streams; this is a paper mechanism, not a current vLLM integration claim.",
    "Evaluation uses Eos H100/Perlmutter A100 historical scientific applications and a CANDLE/FlexFlow DP-only training configuration; strong and weak scaling, steady-state and startup are separate.",
    "The artifact provides Legion source but not all benchmark dependencies; selected hashing skips some fields and leaves an AllReduce TODO. Without tracing-engine checks this is not a universal validity proof or a demonstrated correctness bug."
  ],
